If <MATH_0001> has one of the following properties as an <MATH_0002>-module
<STRUCT_0001>
<ITEMOPEN_0001>(a)<ITEMCLOSE_0001>
finitely generated;
<ITEMOPEN_0002>(b)<ITEMCLOSE_0002>
finitely presented;
<ITEMOPEN_0003>(c)<ITEMCLOSE_0003>
flat;
<ITEMOPEN_0004>(d)<ITEMCLOSE_0004>
faithfully flat;
<ITEMOPEN_0005>(e)<ITEMCLOSE_0005>
finite projective;
<STRUCT_0002>
then so does <MATH_0003> as an <MATH_0004>-module (and conversely).

If <MATH_0001> has one of the following properties as an <MATH_0002>-algebra
<STRUCT_0001>
<ITEMOPEN_0001>(a)<ITEMCLOSE_0001>
of finite type;
<ITEMOPEN_0002>(b)<ITEMCLOSE_0002>
of finite presentation;
<ITEMOPEN_0003>(c)<ITEMCLOSE_0003>
formally unramified;
<ITEMOPEN_0004>(d)<ITEMCLOSE_0004>
unramified;
<ITEMOPEN_0005>(e)<ITEMCLOSE_0005>
<ACCENT_0001>tale;
<STRUCT_0002>
then so does <MATH_0003> as an <MATH_0004>-algebra (and of course conversely).
